Scope-amendment dispatch material, adapted from the runtime-clock kit.

What is here and what it is for
  build-root10-scope-material.mjs   assembles the dispatch material, GitHub verification only
  drive-root10-scope-dispatch.mjs   the trusted caller: fresh observation in, intent/dispatch out
  config.scope.json                 the six Owner merges and the six document paths

What was changed from the runtime-clock originals, and why
  material slot        subject.runtime_clock -> subject.scope_amendment, in both programs
  activation event     sequence 119 / RUNTIME_CLOCK_AMENDMENT_ACTIVATED
                    -> sequence 120 / SCOPE_AMENDMENT_ACTIVATED
  amendment type       Root10RuntimeClockAmendment -> Root10ScopeAmendment
  publications         scope_amendment = PR 204 / f9e1bfc4 (the controller tree and the
                       amendment), acceptance = PR 205 / 26afacff (the stage-2 documents)
  paths                the scope stage-2 documents and Root10ScopeAmendment.json

Verified on 2026-09-16: build-root10-scope-material.mjs emits a complete template against
those merges, and the six fields it leaves for dispatch are operation, ga_raw, observation,
scope_amendment.event, scope_amendment.host_window and the three status_manifest fields.

WHY IT WAS NOT RUN, measured rather than assumed
  clued_control.read_execution() returns 3298514 bytes, and the controller requires the
  observation to be at most 15 seconds old. The driver's own header already ruled out the
  approach I tried: a 3 MB snapshot cannot make a human-mediated round trip inside that
  window. A psql stand-in that relays queries through an out-of-band SQL channel works for
  the small statements and cannot work for this one.

  So the run needs ONE host holding all four at once:
    a real Postgres route to the control store (not an HTTP SQL console)
    Linux Docker, for the qualified container
    gh 2.63.2 at /usr/local/bin/gh -- 2.45.0 from apt does NOT satisfy the byte pin
    /opt/node22/bin/node and /usr/bin/python3.11 at the pinned digests
